At the end of this process, most documents are assigned to latent topics and documents not related to any latent topics are grouped together as an unlabeled topic.
In this study, we computed sentence embeddings using SBERT’s “all-MiniLM-L6-v2”, which is a pre-trained, sentence-transformers model mapping sentences and paragraphs to a 384-dimensional dense vector space [20]. The sentence vector obtained from the allMiniLM-L6-v2 model can be used for clustering or sentence similarity tasks such as topic modeling (for further details, see https://www.sbert.net/docs/pretrained_models.html). To guide the topic modeling process, keywords in Table 1 were used to define anticipated topics based on the ten aspects of professionalism underlying Casper. Default settings in BERTopic were used to perform semi-supervised topic modeling. The BERTopic analyses were conducted using Google Colab Pro+ with a Google Compute Engine backend (GPU). The estimation duration for BERTopic model estimation was around 1 hour.
