4. RESULTS
4.1 Semi-Supervised Text Classification
Table 2 shows the results of the precision and recall values for each professionalism aspect obtained from semi-supervised text classification using the Lbl2vec algorithm. Overall, the results show that precision, recall, and F1 scores are not necessarily very high for the professionalism aspects. This was an anticipated finding because each Casper scenario focuses on a particular aspect (i.e., the intended aspect determined by subject matter experts); however, examinees do not have to focus on the intended aspect underlying each scenario in their responses. In fact, examinees are expected to address multiple aspects of professionalism in their responses since responses to each hypothetical scenario are holistically rated by human raters who do not consider the intended aspect in the marking process.
Although the intended and extracted aspects are not expected to be the same, the results indicated that some aspects identified by the

Lbl2vec algorithm (e.g., collaboration, motivation, communication, and resilience) show a moderate to high alignment with the intended aspects identified by the subject matter experts. Unlike those aspects, detecting problem-solving and empathy was particularly more challenging (i.e., lower alignment with the intended aspects). This finding suggests that the examinees’ written responses to the scenarios related to problem-solving and empathy focused on other aspects of professionalism. In scenarios related to problem-solving and empathy, examinees seemed to focus on selfawareness and resilience in their responses, respectively.
