In addition to the classification results from Lbl2vec, the proportions of professionalism aspects extracted from the responses ranged from 6.4% (empathy) to 15.3% (self-awareness). For aspects where recall was larger than precision (e.g., collaboration, motivation, and resilience), Lbl2vec’s semi-supervised text classification was better at aligning with the intended aspects (i.e., labeling a response as “motivation” for which the same aspect was identified by subject matter experts). In contrast, for the remaining aspects (e.g., communication, empathy, and ethics), the algorithm was better at ruling out the aspects different from the intended aspect (e.g., knowing which responses do not necessarily refer to “empathy” in scenarios where the subject matter experts expected to see other aspects of professionalism).
Overall, the results from the semi-supervised text classification with the Lbl2vec algorithm confirm the multidimensional and complex structure of the professionalism construct [21]. Different behaviors and attributes of professionalism are necessary to address real-life dilemmas and challenges. Furthermore, the findings suggest that Casper offers and delivers on enabling examinees to speak to many aspects of professionalism regardless of the intended aspect identified by the subject matter experts. The confirmation of this feature will guide the Altus team in designing future tests and questions for Casper.
4.2 Semi-Supervised Topic Modeling
Semi-supervised topic modeling analysis with BERTopic indicated that nearly every scenario in Casper was detected as a standalone topic due to the specific context and situation covered in the scenarios. BERTopic identified the aspects underlying each scenario based on the keywords identified within each seed topic representation. On average, each scenario was associated with three aspects of professionalism although there was often a single, dominant aspect underlying some scenarios. Figure 2 shows a bar chart of professionalism aspects assigned by BERTopic for a sample of

