Casper scenarios where each colored bar on the y-axis represents a particular scenario and the x-axis indicates the frequency of responses. Some scenarios focused on multiple aspects (e.g., the orange-colored scenario was related to both professionalism and empathy), whereas others focused on a single aspect (e.g., the yellow-colored scenario was dominantly associated with only selfawareness).

Figure 3 also shows that examinees used similar words and phrases in their responses when responding to scenarios related to some aspects (e.g., problem-solving, resilience, and equity) whereas they used more unique words for other aspects (e.g., motivation). Overall, Figure 3 provides further evidence regarding the possibility of observing more than one aspect of professionalism in examinees’ written responses to the constructed-response items in Casper.
Finally, Figure 4 demonstrates a heatmap of the first 100 scenarios in the dataset. Based on the cosine similarity values between topic embeddings, the heatmap shows the similarity between the extracted topics. Figure 4 shows that most scenarios in the dataset seem to have moderate to high similarities. However, there are some scenarios (see light-green colors) that are quite distinct from the other scenarios based on the words and phrases used by the examinees in their written responses.

